How can I use MATLAB to calculate the number of syllables in each line of Joyce Kilmer's poem "Trees"? Here is the poem for reference:
I think that I shall never see
A poem lovely as a tree.
A tree whose hungry mouth is prest
Against the earth’s sweet flowing breast;
A tree that looks at God all day,
And lifts her leafy arms to pray;
A tree that may in Summer wear
A nest of robins in her hair;
Upon whose bosom snow has lain;
Who intimately lives with rain.
Poems are made by fools like me,
But only God can make a tree.
The formula for calculating the number of syllables in each line is as follows:
Number of syllables = Number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u, y) - Number of diphthongs (two vowels together that make one sound) - Number of silent letters - Number of final "e"s that are not pronounced
To get the number of syllables in each line, I suggest using the following MATLAB code:
poem = ["I think that I shall never see"; 
        "A poem lovely as a tree.";
        "A tree whose hungry mouth is prest";
        "Against the earth’s sweet flowing breast;";
        "A tree that looks at God all day,";
        "And lifts her leafy arms to pray;";
        "A tree that may in Summer wear";
        "A nest of robins in her hair;";
        "Upon whose bosom snow has lain;";
        "Who intimately lives with rain.";
        "Poems are made by fools like me,";
        "But only God can make a tree."];
syllables = zeros(length(poem),1);
for i = 1:length(poem)
    line = lower(poem(i,:));
    vowels = strfind(line, ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u', 'y']);
    diphthongs = strfind(line, {'ae', 'ai', 'au', 'ei', 'eu', 'ie', 'io', 'ou', 'oy', 'ua', 'ue', 'ui'});
    silent_letters = strfind(line, {'h', 'w'});
    final_e = strfind(line, 'e');
    final_e_not_silent = [];
    for j = 1:length(final_e)
        if final_e(j) ~= length(line) && ~ismember(final_e(j), vowels) && ~ismember(final_e(j), diphthongs)
            final_e_not_silent = [final_e_not_silent, final_e(j)];
        end
    end
    syllables(i) = length(vowels) - length(diphthongs) - length(silent_letters) - length(final_e_not_silent);
end
disp(syllables);
This code should output the number of syllables in each line of the poem.

Suppose I have a list of nouns as shown in the Excel table below:
