\begin{equation}
C = \frac{5}{9}(F - 32)
\end{equation}
where C is the temperature in Celsius and F is the temperature in Fahrenheit.
To calculate the average temperature in Celsius for the given list of temperatures, we can use the following formula:
\begin{equation}
\bar{C} = \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{5}{9}(F_i - 32)
\end{equation}
where $\bar{C}$ is the average temperature in Celsius, $n$ is the number of temperature readings in the dataset, and $F_i$ is the temperature in Fahrenheit for the $i$th reading.
