What is the Scala implementation of the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm to generate prime numbers between a given range? Please provide the algorithm formula along with the corresponding Scala code for its implementation.
Algorithm Formula:
1. Create a boolean array to hold the prime numbers, initially set all values to true.
2. Iterate through the array from 2 to the square root of the upper bound.
3. For each prime number found, iterate through its multiples and mark them as not prime in the boolean array.
4. Return all the prime numbers that remain marked as true in the boolean array.
Scala Code:
def sieveOfEratosthenes(n: Int): List[Int] = {
  val primes = Array.fill(n+1)(true)
  primes(0) = false
  primes(1) = false
  for(i <- 2 to Math.sqrt(n).toInt){
    if(primes(i)){
      for(j <- i*i to n by i){
        primes(j) = false
      }
    }
  }
  primes.zipWithIndex.collect{
    case (true, prime) => prime
  }.toList
}
val primes = sieveOfEratosthenes(20)
println(primes)  //output: List(2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19)

