Here is an example MATLAB code that uses the Naive Bayes algorithm to classify the text documents in your dataset:
```
% Load the dataset
data = readtable('dataset_file.tsv', 'Delimiter', '\t');
% Split the dataset into training and testing sets
cvp = cvpartition(height(data), 'HoldOut', 0.3);
trainingData = data(training(cvp), :);
testingData = data(test(cvp), :);
% Create a bag of words model
bag = bagOfWords(trainingData.Text);
% Train a Naive Bayes classifier
classifier = fitcnb(bag, trainingData.Classification);
% Predict the class labels for the testing set
predictedLabels = predict(classifier, testingData.Text);
% Calculate the accuracy of the classifier
accuracy = sum(predictedLabels == testingData.Classification) / length(predictedLabels);
% Display the accuracy
disp(['Accuracy: ', num2str(accuracy)]);
```
